---
import PageLayout from "@/layouts/PageLayout.astro";
import { siteData } from "@/data/site";
import { formatDate } from "@/lib/posts";

const { name, social, legalUpdated } = siteData;
const updated = formatDate(new Date(`${legalUpdated}T00:00:00${siteData.timezoneOffset}`));
---

<PageLayout
	title="How We Research, Verify and Update Our Guides"
	description="How Pinoy Techie researches, verifies and updates its guides, how AI is used and checked, where the facts come from, and how to report a mistake."
	lead={`Last reviewed ${updated}`}
	path="/editorial-policy/"
	dateModified={`${legalUpdated}T00:00:00${siteData.timezoneOffset}`}>
	<p>
		{name} publishes plain-language guides on banks, e-wallets and internet providers in the Philippines. Choices about money and mobile plans
		affect real people, so this page explains the standard we hold our guides to.
	</p>

	<h2>Where our facts come from</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>The official apps and websites of the bank, e-wallet or provider, for rates, fees, limits, plans and rules.</li>
		<li>Regulators and the law, such as the Bangko Sentral ng Pilipinas (BSP), the PDIC, the National Telecommunications Commission (NTC) and the text of Republic Acts.</li>
		<li>Company announcements and newsrooms, and dated reports from reputable news outlets.</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		We keep a list of verified facts together with the date we last checked them, and our guides draw on it. When a figure is not confirmed, a guide
		says to check the official app instead of guessing.
	</p>

	<h2>How a guide is made</h2>
	<ol>
		<li><strong>Topic.</strong> We choose topics from the questions readers ask and from what people search for, not from what pays the most.</li>
		<li><strong>Draft.</strong> A guide is written by us or drafted with AI assistance (see below).</li>
		<li><strong>Fact check.</strong> Numbers, dates and claims are matched against our verified facts and the official sources above.</li>
		<li><strong>Review.</strong> A person reads each AI-assisted guide before it is published.</li>
		<li><strong>Dates and sources.</strong> Every guide shows when it was published and, if it changed, when it was last updated. Guides that rely on official pages list them under "Sources".</li>
	</ol>

	<h2 id="ai-assisted">How we use AI, and how we check it</h2>
	<p>
		Some guides are drafted with the help of AI. They say "By Pinoy Techie via AI" under the title. AI can get facts wrong, so we set rules for it:
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li>It may only use facts from our verified list and from guides we have already published. It is told never to invent prices, plan names, speeds, codes, links or contact details.</li>
		<li>Any peso amount, percentage, speed or code in a draft that we cannot match to our verified facts is flagged, and that draft is held back until a person checks it.</li>
		<li>Every AI-assisted guide ends with a "Sources" list. The sources come from a fixed list of official websites (the company the guide is about, and regulators such as the BSP, PDIC, BIR, NTC and DICT). The AI can only pick from that list and cannot add links of its own. A guide with no valid source is held back.</li>
		<li>Links that are not on our approved list, and invented "Sources" sections, are removed automatically.</li>
		<li>A person reads the guide before it is published.</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		We do not use AI to make up personal experience. If a guide does not say that we tested something ourselves, we have not. Even with these
		checks, an AI-generated guide can contain mistakes, so confirm rates, fees and plans in the official app or website before you decide.
	</p>

	<h2>Keeping guides up to date</h2>
	<p>
		Rates, fees, plans and promos change often. When we notice an official change, or a reader tells us about one, we update the guide and show the
		new "Updated" date. Guides are not a replacement for the provider's own current terms.
	</p>

	<h2>Corrections</h2>
	<p>
		Found a mistake in a guide or a video? <a href="/contact/">Tell us</a>{social.email && <> or email <a href={`mailto:${social.email}`}>{social.email}</a></>}.
		We will check it, fix it and note the update date.
	</p>

	<h2>Independence and how we earn</h2>
	<p>
		{name} is independent and is not affiliated with or endorsed by the companies we write about. This site shows no ads. Where a guide links to
		something we may earn a reward from, such as a referral code, we say so, and the <a href="/disclosure/">referral disclosure</a> explains how it works
		and why it does not change what we write. Nothing on this site is financial advice.
	</p>

	<h2>Who is behind this site</h2>
	<p>
		{name} is an independent Philippine channel and website. Learn more on the <a href="/about/">About page</a>.
	</p>
</PageLayout>
